+// The Archive screen (E14d.2, design 5 "E14d spec"): the tabs this profile
+// closed, newest first, under a header per day (Today, Yesterday, then dates),
+// each row the page's icon and its name. Opened from "Archive" on the rail's
+// "+" menu, as a bubble on the rail (the owner's choice, 2026-09-28), like
+// the rail's other three.
+//
+//   [ Search archive              ]  [ ] All workspaces
+//   Today
+//     (icon) A page
+//   Yesterday
+//     (icon) Another page
+//   ...
+//   [ Clear all ]
+//
+// - Shows the entries of this window's workspace (ResolveTabGuid: a deleted
+//   workspace's entries are Home's, design 2.4); "All workspaces", off at every
+//   open, shows every entry, each row then led by its workspace's rail mark
+//   (WorkspaceRailView::ButtonText) and its tooltip naming the workspace.
+// - The search box filters as it is typed: MatchesQuery() over SearchTextFor()
+//   (workspace_archive.h). Rows and headers are hidden, never rebuilt, so a
+//   keystroke costs one layout.
+// - The list never gets shorter while the screen is open (ApplyFilter): the
+//   bubble sits above the rail with its bottom edge fixed, so a shrinking list
+//   would move the search box under the typing. Its empty-list line is inside
+//   the list for the same reason.
+// - A click, Enter or Space on a row, or Restore on its menu, restores the
+//   page and closes the screen: the window switches to the entry's workspace
+//   (Home for a deleted one, WorkspaceService::EnterWorkspaceForInsert), the
+//   page opens at the top of the list (E15c.1's place), selected and loaded,
+//   with its custom name -- by the road a pinned item opens
