+//   (ArchiveStore::RemoveSince(base::Time())), whatever the switch shows.
+//
+// Every row of the store is built once, off the widget, and attached with one
+// SetContents (E15b: adding children under a layered ancestor walks the whole
+// subtree per add). A change to the store while the screen is open (a Delete,
+// a close in another window, the load finishing) posts ONE rebuild, never runs
+// it inside the store's callback: that can be inside TabStripModel's close. A
+// rebuild keeps the search text, the switch and the scroll offset.
+//
+// Logs, never an address, a title or the search text (47's rule: a log is
+// pasted when asking for help):
+//   "[workspaces] archive screen: opened, N entr(ies), M shown, in T ms"
+//   "[workspaces] archive screen: filter of L char(s) -> M shown in T ms"
